{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"我先把目标文件直接按新题描述实现为独立可运行代码，并在其中加入 `main(grid)` 与 `generate_input()`；随后按你给的自检命令跑 100 次随机样本校验。"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed558458950/2 && cat > /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed558458950/2/5.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Fill the rooms of a tree maze from the start room to the dead-end room by the\nsequence of door colors encountered along that path.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black interior background with rectangular rooms split by one-cell grey walls.\n- Rooms are connected as a tree graph; start room contains one unique maroon pixel.\n- A gate appears as a pair of same-colored pixels on opposite sides of a wall\n  gap, the color is one of a small palette.\n- Start room marker and all gate pixels are not black background.\n\nRule:\n- Identify all room cells (black + maroon), build each room as a component and\n  build door edges from same-color marker pairs separated by one-gap black cell.\n- Find the start room, then follow the unique room graph path to a leaf room.\n- Record gate colors in that traversal order and assign them cyclically to rooms on\n  the path: room i uses color[(i) mod len(sequence)].\n- Repaint only black cells in each visited room with the assigned color; keep\n  maroon and gate pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Doors are the only cross-room clues: marker pairs determine traversal order,\n  and that ordered palette is then reused to recolor the rooms on that path.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\nfrom collections import deque, defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict, Set\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nBG = 0\nWALL = 5\nMAROON = 9\nDOOR_PALETTE = (1, 2, 3, 4, 6)\n\n_DIR4 = ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1))\n\n\ndef _connected_components(mask: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[List[List[Tuple[int, int]]], np.ndarray]:\n    h, w = mask.shape\n    comp_id = -np.ones((h, w), dtype=np.int32)\n    comps: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]] = []\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if not mask[r, c] or comp_id[r, c] \"'!= -1:\n                continue\n            cid = len(comps)\n            q = deque([(r, c)])\n            comp_id[r, c] = cid\n            cells: List[Tuple[int, int]] = [(r, c)]\n            while q:\n                rr, cc = q.popleft()\n                for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n                    nr, nc = rr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if nr < 0 or nr >= h or nc < 0 or nc >= w:\n                        continue\n                    if not mask[nr, nc] or comp_id[nr, nc] != -1:\n                        continue\n                    comp_id[nr, nc] = cid\n                    q.append((nr, nc))\n                    cells.append((nr, nc))\n            comps.append(cells)\n    return comps, comp_id\n\n\ndef _safe_unique_color(grid: np.ndarray) -> int | None:\n    vals, counts = np.unique(grid, return_counts=True)\n    if len(vals) == 0:\n        return None\n    bg = vals[np.argmax(counts)]\n    candidates = [v for v, _ in zip(vals, counts) if v != bg]\n    if not candidates:\n        return None\n    if counts.size == 1:\n        return None\n    # unique maroon-like marker is the only singleton not equal to bg/wall\n    for idx, v in enumerate(vals):\n        if v == bg:\n            continue\n        if counts[idx] == 1:\n            return int(v)\n    return None\n\n\ndef _pair_door_markers(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, wall: int, start_color: int | None) -> List[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int], int]]:\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    pairs: List[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int], int]] = []\n    blocked = set()\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            v = int(grid[r, c])\n            if v == bg or v == wall or (start_color is not None and v == start_color):\n                continue\n            if (r, c) in blocked:\n                continue\n            for dr, dc in ((1, 0), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (0, -1)):\n                rr, cc = r + 2 * dr, c + 2 * dc\n                if rr < 0 or rr >= h or cc < 0 or cc >= w:\n                    continue\n                if (rr, cc) in blocked:\n                    continue\n                if int(grid[rr, cc]) != v:\n                    continue\n                mr, mc = r + dr, c + dc\n                if grid[mr, mc] != bg:\n                    continue\n                a = (r, c)\n                b = (rr, cc)\n                if a < b:\n                    pairs.append((a, b, v))\n                else:\n                    pairs.append((b, a, v))\n                blocked.add(a)\n                blocked.add(b)\n                break\n    return pairs\n\n\ndef _room_components(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, start_color: int | None) -> Tuple[List[List[Tuple[int, int]]], np.ndarray]:\n    mask = grid == bg\n    if start_color is not None:\n        mask = np.logical_or(mask, grid == start_color)\n    comps, comp_id = _connected_components(mask)\n    room_id_map = -np.ones(comp_id.shape, dtype=np.int32)\n    rooms: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]] = []\n    for cid, cells in enumerate(comps):\n        # each room is at least 2x2 => area >=4\n        if len(cells) < 4:\n            continue\n        rid = len(rooms)\n        for rr, cc in cells:\n            room_id_map[rr, cc] = rid\n        rooms.append(cells)\n    return rooms, room_id_map\n\n\ndef _build_room_graph(\n    grid: np.ndarray,\n    rooms: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]],\n    room_id_map: np.ndarray,\n    bg: int,\n    wall: int,\n    start_color: int | None,\n) -> Tuple[Dict[int, Set[int]], Dict[Tuple[int, int], List[int]]]:\n    adj: Dict[int, Set[int]] = {i: set() for i in range(len(rooms))}\n    edge_colors: Dict[Tuple[int, int], List[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n\n    pairs = _pair_door_markers(grid, bg, wall, start_color)\n    h, w = grid.shape\n\n    def marker_room(r: int, c: int) -> int | None:\n        candidates = set()\n        for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if nr < 0 or nr >= h or nc < 0 or nc >= w:\n                continue\n            rid = int(room_id_map[nr, nc])\n            if rid >= 0:\n                candidates.add(rid)\n        for rid in candidates:\n            if len(rooms[rid]) >= 4:\n                return rid\n        return None\n\n    for (r1, c1), (r2, c2), color in pairs:\n        ra = marker_room(r1, c1)\n        rb = marker_room(r2, c2)\n        if ra is None or rb is None or ra == rb:\n            continue\n        a, b = sorted((int(ra), int(rb)))\n        adj[a].add(b)\n        adj[b].add(a)\n        edge_colors[(a, b)].append(int(color))\n\n    return adj, edge_colors\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    grid = np.array(grid, copy=True)\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    if grid.ndim != 2 or h == 0 or w == 0:\n        return grid\n\n    vals, counts = np.unique(grid, return_counts=True)\n    bg = int(vals[np.argmax(counts)])\n    wall_candidates = [(int(v), int(c)) for v, c in zip(vals, counts) if int(v) != bg]\n    if wall_candidates:\n        wall = max(wall_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0]\n    else:\n        wall = int(bg)\n\n    start_color = _safe_unique_color(grid)\n\n    rooms, room_id_map = _room_components(grid, bg, start_color)\n    if len(rooms) <= 1:\n        return grid\n\n    if start_color is None:\n        return grid\n\n    start_room = -1\n    for i, coords in enumerate(rooms):\n        if any(grid[r, c] == start_color for r, c in coords):\n            start_room = i\n            break\n    if start_room < 0:\n        return grid\n\n    adj, edge_colors = _build_room_graph(grid, rooms, room_id_map, bg, wall, start_color)\n    if start_room not in adj:\n        return grid\n\n    # choose one end leaf (a degree<=1 room) not equal to start whenever possible\n    leaves = [rid for rid in range(len(rooms)) if len(adj[rid]) <= 1]\n    if leaves:\n        candidates = [rid for rid in leaves if rid != start_room]\n        if candidates:\n            target = min(candidates)\n        else:\n            target = start_room\n    else:\n        target = None\n\n    # walk from start to target through the room graph (works for generated inputs as a tree-path)\n    path = [start_room]\n    prev = -1\n    cur = start_room\n    seen = {start_room}\n    while target is not None and cur != target:\n        nxts = [n for n in sorted(adj[cur]) if n != prev]\n        # If branch occurs in non-generator inputs, take a deterministic first unvisited route.\n        nxt = None\n        for v in nxts:\n            if v not in seen:\n                nxt = v\n                break\n        if nxt is None:\n            break\n        path.append(nxt)\n        seen.add(nxt)\n        prev, cur = cur, nxt\n\n    if len(path) <= 1:\n        return grid\n\n    color_seq: List[int] = []\n    for a, b in zip(path, path[1:]):\n        key = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n        colors = edge_colors.get(key)\n        if colors:\n            color_seq.append(colors[0])\n\n    if not color_seq:\n        return grid\n\n    out = np.array(grid, copy=True)\n    for i, rid in enumerate(path):\n        color = color_seq[i % len(color_seq)]\n        for rr, cc in rooms[rid]:\n            cell = int(out[rr, cc])\n            if cell == bg or cell == start_color:\n                out[rr, cc] = color\n\n    return out\n\n\ndef _random_path(rng: np.random.Generator, rows: int, cols: int, target_len: int) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    if rows <= 0 or cols <= 0:\n        return []\n    start = (int(rng.integers(rows)), int(rng.integers(cols)))\n    path = [start]\n    used = {start}\n    while len(path) < target_len:\n        r, c = path[-1]\n        candidates = []\n        for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if nr < 0 or nr >= rows or nc < 0 or nc >= cols:\n                continue\n            if (nr, nc) in used:\n                continue\n            candidates.append((nr, nc))\n        if not candidates:\n            break\n        nr, nc = candidates[int(rng.integers(len(candidates)))]\n        used.add((nr, nc))\n        path.append((nr, nc))\n    return path\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n\n    for _ in range(200):\n        slot_rows = int(rng.integers(2, 5))\n        slot_cols = int(rng.integers(2, 5))\n        target_rooms = int(rng.integers(3, 8))\n\n        path = _random_path(rng, slot_rows, slot_cols, target_rooms)\n        if len(path) < 3:\n            continue\n\n        room_h = int(rng.integers(3, 5))\n        room_w = int(rng.integers(3, 5))\n\n        min_r = min(r for r, _ in path)\n        min_c = min(c for _, c in path)\n\n        rows_slots = max(r for r, _ in path) - min_r + 1\n        cols_slots = max(c for _, c in path) - min_c + 1\n\n        h = rows_slots * (room_h + 1) + 1\n        w = cols_slots * (room_w + 1) + 1\n\n        if h > 30 or w > 30:\n            continue\n\n        grid = np.full((h, w), BG, dtype=int)\n\n        # outer boundary walls\n        grid[0, :] = WALL\n        grid[-1, :] = WALL\n        grid[:, 0] = WALL\n        grid[:, -1] = WALL\n\n        slot_to_pos: Dict[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]] = {}\n\n        for r_slot, c_slot in path:\n            rr = r_slot - min_r\n            cc = c_slot - min_c\n            top = 1 + rr * (room_h + 1)\n            left = 1 + cc * (room_w + 1)\n            slot_to_pos[(r_slot, c_slot)] = (top, left)\n            # draw room perimeter walls\n            bottom = top + room_h - 1\n            right = left + room_w - 1\n\n            # room border walls\n            grid[top - 1, left - 1 : right + 2] = WALL\n            grid[bottom + 1, left - 1 : right + 2] = WALL\n            grid[top - 1 : bottom + 2, left - 1] = WALL\n            grid[top - 1 : bottom + 2, right + 1] = WALL\n\n        # mark start room\n        sr, sc = slot_to_pos[path[0]]\n        grid[sr + room_h // 2, sc + room_w // 2] = MAROON\n\n        # carve doors and mark paired gate colors\n        for idx in range(len(path) - 1):\n            p0 = path[idx]\n            p1 = path[idx + 1]\n            c0 = int(rng.choice(DOOR_PALETTE))\n\n            r0, c0_pos = slot_to_pos[p0]\n            r1, c1_pos = slot_to_pos[p1]\n\n            if r0 == r1:\n                # horizontal adjacency\n                row_idx = int(rng.integers(room_h))\n                r_wall = r0 + row_idx\n                c_gap = 1 + min(c0_pos // (room_w + 1), c1_pos // (room_w + 1)) * (room_w + 1) + room_w\n                r_gap = 1 + (r0 - min_r) * (room_h + 1) + row_idx\n\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap] = BG  # opened gap\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap - 1] = c0\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap + 1] = c0\n            else:\n                # vertical adjacency\n                col_idx = int(rng.integers(room_w))\n                c_gap = c0_pos + col_idx\n                r_gap = 1 + min(r0, r1) * (room_h + 1) + room_h\n\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap] = BG\n                grid[r_gap - 1, c_gap] = c0\n                grid[r_gap + 1, c_gap] = c0\n\n        return grid\n\n    # fallback deterministic minimal path\n    return np.array(\n        [\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, MAROON, BG, WALL, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, DOOR_PALETTE[0], BG, DOOR_PALETTE[0], BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, BG, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n        ],\n        dtype=int,\n    )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sample = generate_input()\n    print(sample)\n    print(main(sample))\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"mkdir -p /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed558458950/2 && cat > /home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/code/eval_new/seed558458950/2/5.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Fill the rooms of a tree maze from the start room to the dead-end room by the\nsequence of door colors encountered along that path.\n\nInput structure:\n- Black interior background with rectangular rooms split by one-cell grey walls.\n- Rooms are connected as a tree graph; start room contains one unique maroon pixel.\n- A gate appears as a pair of same-colored pixels on opposite sides of a wall\n  gap, the color is one of a small palette.\n- Start room marker and all gate pixels are not black background.\n\nRule:\n- Identify all room cells (black + maroon), build each room as a component and\n  build door edges from same-color marker pairs separated by one-gap black cell.\n- Find the start room, then follow the unique room graph path to a leaf room.\n- Record gate colors in that traversal order and assign them cyclically to rooms on\n  the path: room i uses color[(i) mod len(sequence)].\n- Repaint only black cells in each visited room with the assigned color; keep\n  maroon and gate pixels unchanged.\n\nKey insight:\n- Doors are the only cross-room clues: marker pairs determine traversal order,\n  and that ordered palette is then reused to recolor the rooms on that path.\n\\\"\\\"\\\"\n\nfrom collections import deque, defaultdict\nfrom typing import List, Tuple, Dict, Set\n\nimport numpy as np\n\nBG = 0\nWALL = 5\nMAROON = 9\nDOOR_PALETTE = (1, 2, 3, 4, 6)\n\n_DIR4 = ((1, 0), (-1, 0), (0, 1), (0, -1))\n\n\ndef _connected_components(mask: np.ndarray) -> Tuple[List[List[Tuple[int, int]]], np.ndarray]:\n    h, w = mask.shape\n    comp_id = -np.ones((h, w), dtype=np.int32)\n    comps: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]] = []\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            if not mask[r, c] or comp_id[r, c] \"'!= -1:\n                continue\n            cid = len(comps)\n            q = deque([(r, c)])\n            comp_id[r, c] = cid\n            cells: List[Tuple[int, int]] = [(r, c)]\n            while q:\n                rr, cc = q.popleft()\n                for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n                    nr, nc = rr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if nr < 0 or nr >= h or nc < 0 or nc >= w:\n                        continue\n                    if not mask[nr, nc] or comp_id[nr, nc] != -1:\n                        continue\n                    comp_id[nr, nc] = cid\n                    q.append((nr, nc))\n                    cells.append((nr, nc))\n            comps.append(cells)\n    return comps, comp_id\n\n\ndef _safe_unique_color(grid: np.ndarray) -> int | None:\n    vals, counts = np.unique(grid, return_counts=True)\n    if len(vals) == 0:\n        return None\n    bg = vals[np.argmax(counts)]\n    candidates = [v for v, _ in zip(vals, counts) if v != bg]\n    if not candidates:\n        return None\n    if counts.size == 1:\n        return None\n    # unique maroon-like marker is the only singleton not equal to bg/wall\n    for idx, v in enumerate(vals):\n        if v == bg:\n            continue\n        if counts[idx] == 1:\n            return int(v)\n    return None\n\n\ndef _pair_door_markers(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, wall: int, start_color: int | None) -> List[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int], int]]:\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    pairs: List[Tuple[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int], int]] = []\n    blocked = set()\n    for r in range(h):\n        for c in range(w):\n            v = int(grid[r, c])\n            if v == bg or v == wall or (start_color is not None and v == start_color):\n                continue\n            if (r, c) in blocked:\n                continue\n            for dr, dc in ((1, 0), (0, 1), (-1, 0), (0, -1)):\n                rr, cc = r + 2 * dr, c + 2 * dc\n                if rr < 0 or rr >= h or cc < 0 or cc >= w:\n                    continue\n                if (rr, cc) in blocked:\n                    continue\n                if int(grid[rr, cc]) != v:\n                    continue\n                mr, mc = r + dr, c + dc\n                if grid[mr, mc] != bg:\n                    continue\n                a = (r, c)\n                b = (rr, cc)\n                if a < b:\n                    pairs.append((a, b, v))\n                else:\n                    pairs.append((b, a, v))\n                blocked.add(a)\n                blocked.add(b)\n                break\n    return pairs\n\n\ndef _room_components(grid: np.ndarray, bg: int, start_color: int | None) -> Tuple[List[List[Tuple[int, int]]], np.ndarray]:\n    mask = grid == bg\n    if start_color is not None:\n        mask = np.logical_or(mask, grid == start_color)\n    comps, comp_id = _connected_components(mask)\n    room_id_map = -np.ones(comp_id.shape, dtype=np.int32)\n    rooms: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]] = []\n    for cid, cells in enumerate(comps):\n        # each room is at least 2x2 => area >=4\n        if len(cells) < 4:\n            continue\n        rid = len(rooms)\n        for rr, cc in cells:\n            room_id_map[rr, cc] = rid\n        rooms.append(cells)\n    return rooms, room_id_map\n\n\ndef _build_room_graph(\n    grid: np.ndarray,\n    rooms: List[List[Tuple[int, int]]],\n    room_id_map: np.ndarray,\n    bg: int,\n    wall: int,\n    start_color: int | None,\n) -> Tuple[Dict[int, Set[int]], Dict[Tuple[int, int], List[int]]]:\n    adj: Dict[int, Set[int]] = {i: set() for i in range(len(rooms))}\n    edge_colors: Dict[Tuple[int, int], List[int]] = defaultdict(list)\n\n    pairs = _pair_door_markers(grid, bg, wall, start_color)\n    h, w = grid.shape\n\n    def marker_room(r: int, c: int) -> int | None:\n        candidates = set()\n        for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if nr < 0 or nr >= h or nc < 0 or nc >= w:\n                continue\n            rid = int(room_id_map[nr, nc])\n            if rid >= 0:\n                candidates.add(rid)\n        for rid in candidates:\n            if len(rooms[rid]) >= 4:\n                return rid\n        return None\n\n    for (r1, c1), (r2, c2), color in pairs:\n        ra = marker_room(r1, c1)\n        rb = marker_room(r2, c2)\n        if ra is None or rb is None or ra == rb:\n            continue\n        a, b = sorted((int(ra), int(rb)))\n        adj[a].add(b)\n        adj[b].add(a)\n        edge_colors[(a, b)].append(int(color))\n\n    return adj, edge_colors\n\n\ndef main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    grid = np.array(grid, copy=True)\n    h, w = grid.shape\n    if grid.ndim != 2 or h == 0 or w == 0:\n        return grid\n\n    vals, counts = np.unique(grid, return_counts=True)\n    bg = int(vals[np.argmax(counts)])\n    wall_candidates = [(int(v), int(c)) for v, c in zip(vals, counts) if int(v) != bg]\n    if wall_candidates:\n        wall = max(wall_candidates, key=lambda x: x[1])[0]\n    else:\n        wall = int(bg)\n\n    start_color = _safe_unique_color(grid)\n\n    rooms, room_id_map = _room_components(grid, bg, start_color)\n    if len(rooms) <= 1:\n        return grid\n\n    if start_color is None:\n        return grid\n\n    start_room = -1\n    for i, coords in enumerate(rooms):\n        if any(grid[r, c] == start_color for r, c in coords):\n            start_room = i\n            break\n    if start_room < 0:\n        return grid\n\n    adj, edge_colors = _build_room_graph(grid, rooms, room_id_map, bg, wall, start_color)\n    if start_room not in adj:\n        return grid\n\n    # choose one end leaf (a degree<=1 room) not equal to start whenever possible\n    leaves = [rid for rid in range(len(rooms)) if len(adj[rid]) <= 1]\n    if leaves:\n        candidates = [rid for rid in leaves if rid != start_room]\n        if candidates:\n            target = min(candidates)\n        else:\n            target = start_room\n    else:\n        target = None\n\n    # walk from start to target through the room graph (works for generated inputs as a tree-path)\n    path = [start_room]\n    prev = -1\n    cur = start_room\n    seen = {start_room}\n    while target is not None and cur != target:\n        nxts = [n for n in sorted(adj[cur]) if n != prev]\n        # If branch occurs in non-generator inputs, take a deterministic first unvisited route.\n        nxt = None\n        for v in nxts:\n            if v not in seen:\n                nxt = v\n                break\n        if nxt is None:\n            break\n        path.append(nxt)\n        seen.add(nxt)\n        prev, cur = cur, nxt\n\n    if len(path) <= 1:\n        return grid\n\n    color_seq: List[int] = []\n    for a, b in zip(path, path[1:]):\n        key = (a, b) if a < b else (b, a)\n        colors = edge_colors.get(key)\n        if colors:\n            color_seq.append(colors[0])\n\n    if not color_seq:\n        return grid\n\n    out = np.array(grid, copy=True)\n    for i, rid in enumerate(path):\n        color = color_seq[i % len(color_seq)]\n        for rr, cc in rooms[rid]:\n            cell = int(out[rr, cc])\n            if cell == bg or cell == start_color:\n                out[rr, cc] = color\n\n    return out\n\n\ndef _random_path(rng: np.random.Generator, rows: int, cols: int, target_len: int) -> List[Tuple[int, int]]:\n    if rows <= 0 or cols <= 0:\n        return []\n    start = (int(rng.integers(rows)), int(rng.integers(cols)))\n    path = [start]\n    used = {start}\n    while len(path) < target_len:\n        r, c = path[-1]\n        candidates = []\n        for dr, dc in _DIR4:\n            nr, nc = r + dr, c + dc\n            if nr < 0 or nr >= rows or nc < 0 or nc >= cols:\n                continue\n            if (nr, nc) in used:\n                continue\n            candidates.append((nr, nc))\n        if not candidates:\n            break\n        nr, nc = candidates[int(rng.integers(len(candidates)))]\n        used.add((nr, nc))\n        path.append((nr, nc))\n    return path\n\n\ndef generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n    rng = np.random.default_rng()\n\n    for _ in range(200):\n        slot_rows = int(rng.integers(2, 5))\n        slot_cols = int(rng.integers(2, 5))\n        target_rooms = int(rng.integers(3, 8))\n\n        path = _random_path(rng, slot_rows, slot_cols, target_rooms)\n        if len(path) < 3:\n            continue\n\n        room_h = int(rng.integers(3, 5))\n        room_w = int(rng.integers(3, 5))\n\n        min_r = min(r for r, _ in path)\n        min_c = min(c for _, c in path)\n\n        rows_slots = max(r for r, _ in path) - min_r + 1\n        cols_slots = max(c for _, c in path) - min_c + 1\n\n        h = rows_slots * (room_h + 1) + 1\n        w = cols_slots * (room_w + 1) + 1\n\n        if h > 30 or w > 30:\n            continue\n\n        grid = np.full((h, w), BG, dtype=int)\n\n        # outer boundary walls\n        grid[0, :] = WALL\n        grid[-1, :] = WALL\n        grid[:, 0] = WALL\n        grid[:, -1] = WALL\n\n        slot_to_pos: Dict[Tuple[int, int], Tuple[int, int]] = {}\n\n        for r_slot, c_slot in path:\n            rr = r_slot - min_r\n            cc = c_slot - min_c\n            top = 1 + rr * (room_h + 1)\n            left = 1 + cc * (room_w + 1)\n            slot_to_pos[(r_slot, c_slot)] = (top, left)\n            # draw room perimeter walls\n            bottom = top + room_h - 1\n            right = left + room_w - 1\n\n            # room border walls\n            grid[top - 1, left - 1 : right + 2] = WALL\n            grid[bottom + 1, left - 1 : right + 2] = WALL\n            grid[top - 1 : bottom + 2, left - 1] = WALL\n            grid[top - 1 : bottom + 2, right + 1] = WALL\n\n        # mark start room\n        sr, sc = slot_to_pos[path[0]]\n        grid[sr + room_h // 2, sc + room_w // 2] = MAROON\n\n        # carve doors and mark paired gate colors\n        for idx in range(len(path) - 1):\n            p0 = path[idx]\n            p1 = path[idx + 1]\n            c0 = int(rng.choice(DOOR_PALETTE))\n\n            r0, c0_pos = slot_to_pos[p0]\n            r1, c1_pos = slot_to_pos[p1]\n\n            if r0 == r1:\n                # horizontal adjacency\n                row_idx = int(rng.integers(room_h))\n                r_wall = r0 + row_idx\n                c_gap = 1 + min(c0_pos // (room_w + 1), c1_pos // (room_w + 1)) * (room_w + 1) + room_w\n                r_gap = 1 + (r0 - min_r) * (room_h + 1) + row_idx\n\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap] = BG  # opened gap\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap - 1] = c0\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap + 1] = c0\n            else:\n                # vertical adjacency\n                col_idx = int(rng.integers(room_w))\n                c_gap = c0_pos + col_idx\n                r_gap = 1 + min(r0, r1) * (room_h + 1) + room_h\n\n                grid[r_gap, c_gap] = BG\n                grid[r_gap - 1, c_gap] = c0\n                grid[r_gap + 1, c_gap] = c0\n\n        return grid\n\n    # fallback deterministic minimal path\n    return np.array(\n        [\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, MAROON, BG, WALL, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, DOOR_PALETTE[0], BG, DOOR_PALETTE[0], BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, BG, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, BG, WALL],\n            [WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL, WALL],\n        ],\n        dtype=int,\n    )\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    sample = generate_input()\n    print(sample)\n    print(main(sample))\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
